      "id": "lpic2-capacity-import-handover",
      "version": 1,
      "track": "LPIC-2",
      "topic": "Capacity planning",
      "unit": "linux-capacity-planning",
      "title": "Repair a capacity plan before the import",
      "summary": "Repair an inherited capacity forecast and deliver a plan that survives known imports before and after the upgrade arrives.",
      "objective": "Repair the inherited archive-volume plan using post-cleanup observations from day 27 onward. Include the latest day 30 and at least 2 days of that period; a one-off cleanup is not continuing negative growth. Retain at least 12582912 KiB (12 GiB) free on every simulated day through day 44. Orders start on day 30 or later; the total quote must fit 160 fictional credits. Account for every published import case and the quote’s arrival date. Keep current data. Use Test plan after repairs; a valid plan may use any supplied affordable quote and date that satisfies all cases.",
      "retry_guidance": "Inspect the policy result and the first failing workload day. Revise the window, quote, date or reserve, then test the whole plan again.",
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "minutes": 30,
      "steps": [
        "Understand the task and supplied observations.",
        "Investigate growth, quotes and lead times.",
        "Test and repair the complete independent plan."
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Use observations from the requested operating period and include the latest sample.",
        "Reserve is unused space; it must remain available before the upgrade arrives as well as afterward.",
        "Inspect every workload and the quote budget. A passing selected case alone is insufficient."
      ],
      "explanation": "One valid repair uses day27–30, rapid-expansion ordered on day30, and12582912KiB reserve. Delivery is on day32 before the day33 import. urgent-expansion is another valid affordable quote. Earlier aggregate decline includes cleanup and is not continuing negative growth; small capacity or late bulk delivery leaves a failure even if another case passes.",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/exam-201-202-objectives/"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Finite supplied volume-occupancy records and fictional quotes; one expansion at the beginning of its arrival day, constant per-case daily growth and explicit one-off additions. Forecasts are assumptions, not measurements of future reality. No host monitoring, disk resize, real order, data deletion, arbitrary expressions or named monitoring-product emulation.",
